for many families talking about the  potential of gun violence in school is  never easy one valley family says while  it's hard it's also necessary to make  your children be alert  just starting the conversation is the  important part joy and phil hoover are  talking about gun violence with their  two young daughters both parents  agreeing dropping off their daughters at  school after hearing about the shooting  at the texas elementary school wasn't  easy their peace of mind knowing both  nine-year-old vivian and five-year-old  ruby are educated on what to do if an  emergency happens  a hard walk down where if that does  happen we like turn off all the lights  we lock all the doors vivian quickly  stepping in to comfort her sister as a  conversation they say can get  overwhelming do you feel  scared  yeah and overwhelmed overwhelmed yeah  sometimes those things happen  psychiatrist dr sid kirana with nevada  mental health says preparation helps  proactive dialogues with parents  teachers and the community are key if  the child is getting more and more  scared or upset by me talking it is time  for me to stop it's time for me to take  a break let them process and digest what  we have said and then let them come back  and be ready for the next round the  hoovers also say being involved in  community events helps their daughters  understand what's happening they say  being proactive works for them i don't  think there's a perfect answer i think  the answer is  what is going to work best for your  family but i think the answer is always  to say something
 

